{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active and your VPN access is turned on, and your work computer is online, so the problem is most likely the VPN connection from home. Please try these steps: 1) Open the VPN client and connect, approving the Duo prompt on your phone. Internal sites like the intranet only load while the VPN shows as connected. 2) Once it shows connected, try the intranet again. If it still won't load, open it in a private/incognito browser window, or clear your browser cache. 3) If the VPN won't connect, quit and reopen the VPN client, then restart your computer, and let us know the exact error message it shows. If the intranet still won't load while the VPN is connected, reply to this ticket and we will pass it to our senior technicians.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (user 11): active, vpn_access true, sign_in_blocked false, 0 failed logins, MFA not an issue. Sign-in logs: VPN sign-ins from residential IP succeed regularly (most recent Fri 10-09), no failed_password or mfa_denied. Device BL-DT-0111 online, last check-in 10-11, 70% disk free, no warnings. Cannot see the live VPN session state, so unclear whether user is connected now. Followed KB-016 quick checks and fix steps (connect VPN, retry, private window/cache clear). Not escalated yet because VPN connection status is unconfirmed. If user confirms VPN connected and internal sites still fail, escalate per KB-016. If VPN won't connect, follow KB-013 (no sign-in or account issues found).",
